2756,448,264,46342,315,220,16,17,14924,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the maximum number of square inches in the area of a rectangle with a perimeter of 12 inches?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"d2c82317492d24d63f64e4d37c6767a740ef1c88e125f61a3c31d3fdd44c1efd"},"seconds":10.005979776382446,"seed":678226587123732545,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the maximum area of a rectangle with a given perimeter of 12 inches, we start by expressing the perimeter and area in terms of the length and width of the rectangle.\n\nLet the length of the rectangle be \\( l \\) and the width be \\( w \\). The perimeter of the rectangle is given by:\n\\[ 2l + 2w = 12 \\]\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\\[ l + w = 6 \\]\nWe can express the width \\( w \\) in terms of the length \\( l \\):\n\\[ w = 6 - l \\]\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of the rectangle is given by:\n\\[ A = l \\cdot w \\]\nSubstituting \\( w = 6 - l \\) into the area formula, we get:\n\\[ A = l (6 - l) = 6l - l^2 \\]\n\nTo find the maximum area, we need to find the vertex of the parabola described by the quadratic equation \\( A = -l^2 + 6l \\). The vertex form of a parabola \\( ax^2 + bx + c \\) has its maximum (or minimum) value at \\( x = -\\frac{b}{2a} \\). Here, \\( a = -1 \\) and \\( b = 6 \\), so:\n\\[ l = -\\frac{6}{2(-1)} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\]\n\nWhen \\( l = 3 \\), the width \\( w \\) is:\n\\[ w = 6 - l = 6 - 3 = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the rectangle is actually a square with side length 3 inches. The area of this square is:\n\\[ A = 3 \\cdot 3 = 9 \\]\n\nTherefore, the maximum number of square inches in the area of the rectangle is:\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:158"}
